  "notes": "Brooklyn/Firm-era luxury-noir over Buckwild and Pete Rock loops — the consonant end of the Queensbridge axis, and the only one here with real jazz turnarounds rather than a vamp. Distinguished by three things: the heaviest swing on this axis, ii–v–i motion with ninth colour, and a bass that genuinely walks (root–3rd–5th–octave) rather than following the kick. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it medium-high and says the specific numbers are catalog-level rather than from a producer interview.",
